 What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- currently an active object in scene shows a toolbar button with a dropdown menu of contextual actions. The menu button however does not look like a (dropdown) button at all.\r\n\r\n- This PR is adding a chevron to convey it's actually a dropdown button:\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n| master | PR |\r\n|--------|---------|\r\n| <img width=\"572\" height=\"282\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-30 at 0 59 05\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb892a91-d144-472a-9cd3-f81859fe54e8\" /> | <img width=\"562\" height=\"292\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-30 at 0 43 07\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/77dc6fc2-d923-48c8-b83d-0983ae3011aa\" /> |\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n- AI helped me to locate the relevant code\r\n\r\n- currently the changes are applied only to `MeshInstance3D`. If this change would be considered suitable for merging, same changes can be applied to other object types.\r\n\r\n- since the button already had an icon, I had to wrap it into a container to to show two icons\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518733,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg3MzM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/usability","name":"usability","description":"","color":"447744","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"ar